NFC Magic ISO15693: the gen1 consent screen says why it has no validation line

Neither consent body reports how well gen1 is validated, and nothing said that
was deliberate -- so the obvious improvement, on a screen where the user agrees
to a destructive write, is to add a reassurance back.

The note at the branch closes that. What the user consents to is the write and
its blast radius, which both bodies state. How well the path is validated is not
something they can act on at that moment, and on a consent screen the one thing
a reassurance can change is whether they say yes.

